## Summary
Armenia's pro-EU prime minister is targeting former rival Robert Kocharyan, who has been detained along with his son in a corruption investigation.

## Key Points
- Former Armenian President Robert Kocharyan and his son were detained in an ongoing corruption probe
- The detention is part of a political move by Armenia's current pro-EU prime minister against a former rival
- The case highlights ongoing political tensions in Armenia between pro-EU and former leadership factions


